id: pm-jev-undefined-choice-admission
title: Count choice options from the JSON request representation
description: "Canonicalize undefined object entries by JSON omission before admission counting and transport. Verify option identities and counts against real SDK loopback request bodies, including empty-choice refusal."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: admission,"gh:unbraind/pm-jev#101"
created_at: "2026-11-06T11:08:48.326Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T11:15:45.947Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T11:10:34.667Z",codex-sol,"Decision: match official SDK JSON serialization by removing undefined object properties in the bounded detached input before schema validation and counting. Null retains an undescribed option; a sole undefined entry becomes empty and refuses before metadata. Compare admitted identities and counts with real SDK loopback requests."
  "2026-11-06T11:15:22.822Z",codex-sol,"Implementation and linked tests pass (2/2). Behavioral revert in a disposable package copy: replacing only parseAdmissionInput with main makes both regressions fail (0/2): admitted count differs from the actual SDK request and sole-undefined choice fails to refuse. Restoring the fix passes (2/2). JSON omission is documented; null preserves an undescribed option and caller objects remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-06T11:15:32.194Z",codex-sol,"Validation: focused admission/reference suite passes 7/7, including actual SDK loopback request bodies; build, build:test, lint, typecheck, docstring and zero-duplication gates pass. Full npm and Bun release gates run in PR CI. No thresholds or dependency pins changed. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
